#!/usr/bin/env python3

"""
UDCPR CANONICAL DATABASE REBUILDER

Authoritative sources
---------------------

1. udcpr_canonical_manifest.json
   - authoritative regulation number
   - authoritative title
   - authoritative printed start page
   - authoritative manifest order
   - generated from complete UDCPR INDEX pages 5-14

2. udcpr_source_chunks.json
   - authoritative extracted regulation text
   - source PDF pages
   - tables belonging to each regulation
   - table markdown / rows / headers

The PDF itself is NOT reparsed for regulation identity here.

This is intentional.

The pipeline is:

    UDCPR.pdf
        |
        +--> build_udcpr_manifest.py
        |       INDEX PDF pages 5-14
        |       -> udcpr_canonical_manifest.json
        |
        +--> build_udcpr_source_chunks.py
                manifest
                + PDF
                -> udcpr_source_chunks.json
        |
        +--> THIS SCRIPT
                source chunks
                -> PostgreSQL

Important behavior
------------------

* All 329 canonical manifest entries are required.
* INDEX pages 5-14 are represented by the manifest.
* 2.2.5(a) and 2.2.5(b) are separate canonical regulations.
* Duplicate numbers such as 10.14 are allowed when title/page occurrence
  differs.
* Multiple regulations on one PDF page are supported.
* One regulation spanning many PDF pages is supported.
* Sub-regulations that are not canonical manifest entries remain inside
  their parent text.
* Tables are persisted against the regulation owning the source chunk.
* Table markdown remains available in the regulation text.
* No ChromaDB modification is performed.
* Dry-run is the default.
* PostgreSQL is modified only with --apply.
"""

